2026-11-07T06:56:21.7971290Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:56:21.7996240Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8001810Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8006780Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8007060Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8007240Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8007550Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8007760Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8008160Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8008390Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8008540Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8008820Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8009140Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8009330Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:56:21.8010160Z   $ sh ./install-nix
